file: manuals/development/
consumers: [developers and technical founders, Mochi and node agents answering "how do I build X with greatVibe?", documentation maintainers]
produces: [technical, procedural developer manual: SDLC turn loop, ACE and context, Git, nodes/builds/tests, DevOps (CI/CD, IaC), agile work management, security and secrets]
---
# Purpose
How to develop software with greatVibe, as greatVibe actually works today.
Agents read `overview.md` first, then one chapter.

# Key Files
- `overview.md` — the dev loop, quick reference, chapter map.
- `turn-lifecycle-and-sdlc.md` — SDLC phases mapped to turns and gvturns.
- `ace-and-context.md` — design-led coding with ACE files and repo context.
- `git-and-repositories.md` — repositories, branches, commits and pushes.
- `nodes-builds-and-tests.md` — where code runs, runtimes, tests, long builds.
- `devops-cicd-and-iac.md` — CI/CD connectors, cloud changes, delivery evidence.
- `agile-work-management.md` — plans, flows, investigations, work items.
- `security-and-secrets.md` — secrets, credentials and risky actions.

# Dependencies
- Links into `../../concepts/`, `../../how-to/` and `../../reference/` rather
  than repeating them.
- `../../SANITIZATION.md` publication boundary.

# Gotchas
- Shipped behaviour only. No features in design, rollout phases, roadmap or
  internal pipelines. Long-term vision belongs in getting-started.
- Every procedure must be something a user or their agent can do today with
  their own permissions. Staff-only support administration is out of scope.
- Use placeholders: `my-service`, `node_example`, `/workspace/my-service`.

# Change History
- 2026-10-12: Created the development manual set.
